			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EQUAL \/ NOT EQUAL\n\nEqual sends out true when the left input equals the right input.\nNot Equal send out true when the left input does not equal the right input.\n\n- Patch Explained - \n\n• The Metronome triggers the Random node at a steady pace.\n• Each time triggered the Random node produces a random value between 0 and 3.\n• The value is passed into both the Equal and Not Equal nodes to be tested.\n• The ouput of the test is send to a switch that ouputs 0.3 if true and 0.6 if false.\n•  These values adjust the width and height of the Rectangle node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 263,
					"width": 747,
					"x": 108.203125,
